## 2. IMPLEMENTATION — on-demand large CNode backing (6 files, base-sel4)

The mechanism reuses Genode's existing 16K untyped pool (the VTX VCPU
pool) and the proven VTX allocation pattern (alloc_pages(phys_alloc_16k,4)
+ _core_local_sel(TOP_CNODE_UNTYPED_16K, phys, 14)). The change is MINIMAL
and COHERENT; non-x86_64 arches are upstream byte-for-byte.

Files changed (all under genode/repos/base-sel4/):

  src/include/base/internal/capability_space_sel4.h
    x86_64 only (gated `#ifdef __x86_64__`): CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2_2ND 7->9.
    1ST stays 6 (1st-level CNode keeps its 4 KiB backing, upstream).
    => per-PD main CSpace 8192 -> 32768 slots.
    Other arches keep the upstream `(CONFIG_WORD_SIZE==32)?8:7` unchanged.

  src/core/include/untyped_memory.h
    + enum { LARGE_BACKING_UNTYPED_LOG2 = 14 };  (the 16K untyped object
      size; = Vcpu_kobj::SIZE_LOG2 on x86_64; inert on arches whose CNodes
      stay page-sized)
    + size-aware `untyped_sel(phys, backing_log2)` overload: routes to
      TOP_CNODE_UNTYPED_16K (phys>>14) when backing > 4 KiB, else the 4K
      default. (Selector addressing verified against the VTX pattern,
      spec/x86/platform_thread.cc:52.)
    + `free_pages(alloc, addr, num_pages)` helper (symmetric with free_page).
    + declaration of per-arch `cnode_backing_alloc(size_log2, default)`.

  src/core/include/cnode.h
    The 4-arg Range_allocator-form `Cnode` ctor (used for every child-PD
    main-CSpace CNode in platform_pd.cc) is now size-aware:
      backing_log2 = Cnode_kobj::SIZE_LOG2(=5) + size_log2
      large        = backing_log2 > PAGE_SIZE_LOG2
      pool         = cnode_backing_alloc(size_log2, phys_alloc)
      _phys        = large ? alloc_pages(pool, 1<<(backing_log2-12))
                           : alloc_page(pool)
      service sel  = large ? untyped_sel(phys, backing_log2)
                           : untyped_sel(phys)
      create<Cnode_kobj>(service, parent_sel, dst_idx, size_log2)
    `destruct` is made size-aware symmetrically (frees to the same pool it
    allocated from). Core's own CNodes use the separate Initial_untyped_pool
    ctor and are unaffected.

  src/core/spec/x86_64/platform.cc
    + `Untyped_memory::cnode_backing_alloc`: returns `phys_alloc_16k()` when
      the CNode backing exceeds one page, else the caller's default.
    + 16K-pool carve `max_pd_mem` enlarged from VCPU-only to also cover
      MAX_CNODE_PD_COUNT(=64) child PDs x (1<<CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2_1ST=64) 2nd-
      level CNodes x 16 KiB = 64 MiB + 256 KiB VCPU. FIXED bounded size.

  src/core/spec/arm/platform.cc, src/core/spec/arm_v8a/platform.cc
    + `cnode_backing_alloc` definition: returns the default allocator
      unchanged (ARM keeps page-sized CNodes; the large-backing branch is
      never taken; defined so the symbol links).

Backed by an `error("Cnode construction failed")` fail-loud gate (cnode.h:
the seL4 retype returns nonzero when the 16K pool is exhausted, _phys is
cleared, constructed() returns false, and platform_pd.cc:176/209 refuse to
install the CNode — bounded, never a silent hang).

