### 3.3 sponge-falkon-disk — reaches vm_space stage (past cspace)

Run: make -C genode/build/x86_64 run/sponge-falkon-disk KERNEL=sel4 BOARD=pc \
     RUN_OPT='--include power_on/qemu --include log/qemu --include image/disk'
Log: docs/evidence/c1-sponge-falkon-disk.log

  5745 MiB RAM and 523288 caps assigned to init
  [init -> system -> falkon_probe] falkon-probe: [3] launch falkon via sponge_pkgd
  [init -> system -> falkon_probe] falkon-probe: [3] launch ok — WebEngine first paint may take minutes under softpipe
  Warning: flush page table entries - mapping cache full - PD: init -> rom_pkg out of selector
  [init -> system -> pkg_runtime -> falkon] lwIP Nic interface up address=10.0.2.15 netmask=255.255.255.0 gateway=10.0.2.2 nameserver=10.0.2.3
  Warning: flush page table entries - mapping cache full - PD: init -> rom_pkg out of selector
  Warning: flush page table entries - mapping cache full - PD: ... -> falkon out of selector
  [init -> system -> pkg_runtime -> falkon] Error: stop because parent denied RM-session: label="", ram_quota=64K, cap_quota=2
  [init -> system -> falkon_probe] Error: falkon-probe: FAIL falkon window never rendered into nitpicker

PROGRESSION CONFIRMED: falkon launches from disk, lwIP DHCPs to 10.0.2.15,
then hits the vm_space "mapping cache full / out of selector" limit (the
C2 blocker — Core::Vm_space NUM_VM_SEL_LOG2=15 => 32768 mappings/PD,
independent of CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2). This is the EXPECTED C2 failure, NOT the
cspace stage: 0x "Cnode construction failed" (16K pool did NOT exhaust);
the main CSpace (32768 slots) carried falkon's launch + DHCP cleanly.
Matches the proven prior-art progression (p4-cspace-fix.log §1 run1).

