## 4. Vendored changes for the docs/11 patch ledger (C4 writes the row)

C4 will add the docs/11-environment.md §4 ledger row. The vendored surface
this workstream introduces (all under genode/repos/base-sel4/, gated to
x86_64 where applicable, other arches upstream byte-for-byte):

  WHAT  : On-demand 16 KiB CNode backing + per-PD main CSpace 8192->32768.
  WHERE : capability_space_sel4.h (CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2_2ND x86_64 7->9);
          untyped_memory.h (size-aware untyped_sel + cnode_backing_alloc decl
          + LARGE_BACKING_UNTYPED_LOG2 + free_pages);
          cnode.h (size-aware Range_allocator ctor + destruct);
          spec/x86_64/platform.cc (cnode_backing_alloc def + 64 MiB carve);
          spec/{arm,arm_v8a}/platform.cc (cnode_backing_alloc def, default).
  WHY   : base-sel4 capped each child-PD CNode at one 4 KiB page (max 128
          slots/CNode, 16384/PD), blocking large workloads (falkon WebEngine)
          at the main CSpace. The 16K-backing path lifts this to 32768/PD
          using the existing VTX 16K untyped pool. dma-safe: the carve is a
          fixed bounded 64 MiB (not proportional to RAM), so it does not
          starve init RAM or disturb the platform-driver/ahci boot chain.
  DROP  : revert the 6 files; upstream base-sel4 behaviour is restored
          (8192-slot page-sized CSpace, 256 KiB VCPU-only 16K pool). When
          upstream Genode grows lazy/size-aware CNodes (the platform.cc:108
          XXX), this patch is obsolete.

